Vibration window size still critically small
→ Reset happens only every ~32 ms → effective averaging window = 1–2 samples
→ RMS ≈ single sample magnitude → defeats the purpose of RMS as energy measure
→ Fix: Implement proper time-based rolling window (1–3 seconds recommended)
Audio frequency estimation is very crude
→ Zero-crossing count (ZCC) works reasonably only for clean, single-tone signals
→ Extremely inaccurate for real-world sounds (speech, music, machinery, noise) due to harmonics, noise, multiple sources
→ Real "noise source identification" requires proper FFT or at least autocorrelation/pitch detection → ZCC gives only rough dominant frequency estimate
dB is relative, not calibrated SPL
→ Current calculation is signal level dBFS (relative to full scale) + arbitrary +90 offset
→ Android microphones have very different sensitivities; no standard SPL calibration
→ Without device-specific calibration (impossible in general app), values are only useful as relative loudness meter
No gravity vector remapping in vibration calculation
→ linX/Y/Z computed from raw gravity → incorrect when phone is rotated (landscape/portrait)
Missing light in UI update throttling
→ processLight updates smoothedLux, but UI only throttled by gyro → possible stale values if light changes without IMU events